## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): This is where all CMS content state is computed and provided to the entire app (236 consumers via useContent). It currently memoizes defaultContent as a static value with no update mechanism — the root cause of why live preview cannot work. Contentstack Live Preview SDK requires the provider to accept real-time content updates and re-render consumers; this is the sole site that controls the content object flowing into context.
  - **Minimal fix:** Replace the static useMemo with useState initialized from defaultContent, and integrate Contentstack Live Preview SDK: (1) Add useState: `const [content, setContent] = useState<IContentstackContent>(defaultContent);` with a useEffect to sync when defaultContent changes on navigation. (2) Initialize Contentstack live preview on the client-side Stack instance (in the SDK init, add `live_preview: { enable: true, preview_token: <from URL params> }`). (3) Subscribe to live preview callback/events and call setContent with the merged updated content so all 236 useContent consumers re-render with preview data. The IContentstackContent interface and ContentstackContext.Provider value shape stay the same — only the source of the content object changes from static memo to live-updating state.


